#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_bom.rst:5
msgid "Bill of Materials"
msgstr "Bill of Materials"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_bom.rst:7
msgid ""
"**Bill of Materials** is what has to be procured in order to have the "
"object: every line item, counted. It is :doc:`/config_bom` as a tab, and the"
" same answer ``pc bom`` prints."
msgstr ""
"**Bill of Materials** es lo que hay que abastecer para tener el objeto: cada"
" partida, contada. Es :doc:`/config_bom` como pestaña, y la misma respuesta "
"que imprime ``pc bom``."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_bom.rst:11
msgid ""
"What it is *not* is a list of parts. A part that is made is its **stock** --"
" you buy the sheet, not the panel cut out of it -- and a sub-assembly that "
"declares a ``vendor:`` and an ``sku:`` is one item ordered whole, with "
"nothing inside it looked at. What is built and what is bought comes from "
":doc:`Build vs Buy </digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_bvb>`; where "
"nothing was chosen, a line that can be either is bought."
msgstr ""
"Lo que *no* es, es una lista de piezas. Una pieza que se fabrica es su "
"**stock** -- se compra la plancha, no el panel que se corta de ella -- y un "
"subensamblaje que declara un ``vendor:`` y un ``sku:`` es un solo artículo "
"que se pide entero, sin mirar nada de lo que hay dentro. Qué se fabrica y "
"qué se compra viene de :doc:`Build vs Buy "
"</digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_bvb>`; donde no se eligió nada, una"
" línea que puede ser cualquiera de las dos cosas se compra."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_bom.rst:19
msgid "In the UI"
msgstr "En la interfaz"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_bom.rst:21
msgid ""
"One row per line item, with how many of each. For a part or an assembly."
msgstr ""
"Una fila por partida, con cuántas de cada una. Para una pieza o un "
"ensamblaje."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_bom.rst:23
msgid ""
"The Manufacturing group's Bill of Materials tab: every line item, counted"
msgstr ""
"La pestaña Bill of Materials del grupo Manufacturing: cada partida, contada"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_bom.rst:29
msgid "On the command line"
msgstr "En la línea de comandos"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_bom.rst:37
msgid ""
":doc:`/config_bom` explains how interfaces, ``alias`` and ``enrich`` make a "
"line item interchangeable -- an abstract position in the bill of materials "
"that a concrete part fills."
msgstr ""
":doc:`/config_bom` explica cómo las interfaces, ``alias`` y ``enrich`` hacen"
" intercambiable una partida -- una posición abstracta de la lista de "
"materiales que llena una pieza concreta."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_bom.rst:42
msgid "Agent skills"
msgstr "Skills de agente"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_bom.rst:44
msgid "``/pc:validate``"
msgstr "``/pc:validate``"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_bom.rst:45
msgid ""
"Reads the bill of materials as part of giving a requirement its verdict: a "
"line of it is evidence for a feature that no measurement can judge."
msgstr ""
"Lee la lista de materiales como parte de dar su veredicto a un requisito: "
"una línea de ella es evidencia de una característica que ninguna medición "
"puede juzgar."
